# counter harness. One force call is one clean energy and gradient.
# Noise is added after the call. A repeated coordinate keeps that sample.
# The index uses the clean Hessian. Six rigid modes are removed.
# A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference.
# Default profile. initial_step_size is -1e-7, alpha_min is 1e-3, and eps_subsp is 1e-5. The wrapper constructor uses -0.01 and eps_subsp 1e-3, which let LJ38 leave the cutoff. The stop is the noise-aware force norm, and at positive sigma the clean energy over the last window. The index is the clean Hessian with the rigid-mode rule. Variable-cell SQNM is not on this problem: the spec potential has no cell.
